WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:07.610
- [Narrator] During a vaginal childbirth,

00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:11.120
the first stage of labor
lasts about 12 to 19 hours

00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:15.273
and starts when your baby
settles lower into your pelvis.

00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:19.290
In response, your cervix begins to efface

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:22.723
or become thinner and dilate or widen.

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:27.130
During this time, you may feel
strong regular contractions

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:29.020
occurring at every five to 20 minutes

00:00:30.070 --> 00:00:33.650
and lower back pain and
cramping that doesn't go away.

00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:36.710
You may see a brownish or
reddish mucus discharge

00:00:36.710 --> 00:00:38.160
which could be the mucus plug

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:40.260
at the opening of your cervix falling out.

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:42.840
Your water may break,

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:45.030
which can either be a large gush of fluid

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:46.533
or a continuous trickle.

00:00:47.550 --> 00:00:51.110
If you experience any of these
symptoms, contact your doctor

00:00:51.110 --> 00:00:54.500
or midwife to see if you
should go to the hospital.

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:56.650
At the beginning of stage two of labor,

00:00:56.650 --> 00:00:59.300
which can last from a few
minutes to three hours,

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:02.140
your cervix is fully
dilated to 10 centimeters

00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:04.920
and your baby's head has moved

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:07.803
beyond the cervical opening
into your birth canal.

00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:12.750
During this stage, you will
begin to push your baby out.

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:15.620
You may instinctively push
when you feel the urge,

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:16.880
or you may need coaching

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:19.260
from your doctor, midwife or labor nurse

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:22.450
as to when to push and when to rest.

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:23.690
In a normal delivery,

00:01:23.690 --> 00:01:26.563
your baby's head will
rotate to face your back.

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:29.140
During active labor,

00:01:29.140 --> 00:01:32.160
your uterus is divided
into an active segment

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:35.270
that contracts, pushing the baby downward,

00:01:35.270 --> 00:01:38.520
and a flexible passive
segment that remains relaxed,

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:40.220
stretching to provide more room

00:01:40.220 --> 00:01:41.713
for the baby to pass through.

00:01:43.270 --> 00:01:46.370
In some cases, when the
top of your baby's head

00:01:46.370 --> 00:01:50.560
appears or crowns, your
doctor may make a small cut

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:53.853
called in a episiotomy to
enlarge the vaginal opening.

00:01:54.770 --> 00:01:57.283
Then, you will continue put your baby out.

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:03.040
As your baby's head passes
through the birth canal,

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:06.090
it molds into an elongated shape.

00:02:06.090 --> 00:02:08.530
An elongated head shape
will resolve itself

00:02:08.530 --> 00:02:12.323
within a few days as the skull
bones shift back into place.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:16.903
After your baby's head
exits the birth canal,

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:20.730
his or her head and shoulders will rotate

00:02:20.730 --> 00:02:23.280
to help the shoulders pass
through the birth canal.

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:27.800
Your baby's shoulders are
delivered one after the other

00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:29.603
in order to fit through your pelvis.

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:33.130
Once the shoulders emerge,

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:35.443
the rest of your baby slides out easily.

00:02:38.990 --> 00:02:40.430
After your baby is born,

00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:42.673
his or her umbilical cord will be cut.

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:45.360
In stage three of labor,

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:47.690
which may last five to 30 minutes,

00:02:47.690 --> 00:02:50.140
mild contractions will
help push the placenta

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:51.203
out of the uterus.

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:56.060
During this stage, you and
your baby may begin bonding

00:02:56.060 --> 00:02:59.143
through skin to skin
contact and breastfeeding.

